Follow these steps to setup 2 or more CloudLab nodes with 1 Memcached server and 1 or more Mutilate load generation clients.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Get access to >= 2 CloudLab nodes loaded with Ubuntu 22.04 image.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------

2. Allow nodes ssh access to each other:

Terminal A:                                                   |  Terminal B:
   user@pc:~$  ssh <cloudlab_node_0>                          |     user@pc:~$  ssh <cloudlab_node_1>
   user@node0:~$ ssh-keygen                                   |     user@node1:~$ ssh-keygen
   user@node0:~$ cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub                        |     user@node1:~$
   user@node0:~$                                              |         --> append node0 id_rsa.pub to file ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
      --> append node1 id_rsa.pub to ~/.ssh/authorized_keys   |     user@node1:~$ cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub

-----------------------------------------------------------------------

3. Update Ubuntu package repository and upgrade packages on all nodes:
   user@nodeX:~$ sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

-----------------------------------------------------------------------

4. Download and build Memcached on 1 node:

Terminal A:
   user@node0:~$ sudo apt install -y libevent-dev
   user@node0:~$ wget http://memcached.org/latest	
   user@node0:~$ mkdir memcached
   user@node0:~$ tar -xf latest -C memcached --strip-components=1
   user@node0:~$ cd memcached/
   user@node0:~$ ./configure && make && make test && sudo make install

-----------------------------------------------------------------------

5. Download and build Mutilate on all other nodes:

Terminal Y:
   user@nodeX:~$ sudo apt install -y libevent-dev gengetopt libzmq3-dev
   user@nodeX:~$ sudo apt install -y python2.7
   user@nodeX:~$ wget -P ~/.local/lib https://bootstrap.pypa.io/pip/2.7/get-pip.py
   user@nodeX:~$ python2.7 ~/.local/lib/get-pip.py --user	
   user@nodeX:~$ python2.7 -m pip install --user scons				
   user@nodeX:~$ git clone https://github.com/awadyn/mutilate.git
   user@nodeX:~$ cd mutilate/
   user@nodeX:~$ git checkout develop                         (--> switch to develop branch)
   user@nodeX:~$ make                                         (--> build monloop)
   user@nodeX:~$ python2.7 ~/.local/bin/scons                 (--> build mutilate)
   user@nodeX:~$ g++ -o mutilate monloop.o mutilate.o cmdline.o log.o distributions.o util.o \
                        Connection.o Protocol.o Generator.o -L/opt/local/lib -levent -lpthread -lrt -lzmq

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Testing:
--------

6. Test run Memcached with T threads:

Terminal A:
   user@node0:~$ taskset -c 0-<T-1> ~/memcached/memcached -u nobody -t <T> -m 32G -c 8192 -b 8192 -l 10.10.1.2 -B binary


7. Test run Mutilate agents with 16 threads each:

Terminal Y:
   user@nodeX:~$ ~/mutilate/mutilate --agentmode --threads=16


8. Test run Mutilate master with 1 thread (first, load database):

Terminal B:
   user@nodeX:~$ taskset -c 0 ~/mutilate/mutilate --binary -s 10.10.1.K --loadonly -K fb_key -V fb_value
   user@nodeX:~$ taskset -c 0 ~/mutilate/mutilate --binary -s 10.10.1.K --noload --agent={10.10.1.M,10.10.1.N,10.10.1.P,..} \
                         --threads=1 --keysize=fb_key --valuesize=fb_value --iadist=fb_ia --update=0.25 --depth=4           \
                         --connections=4 --measure_qps=2000 --qps=<QPS> --time=30
